index 2f841f552f..828e3c8c91 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -75,6 +75,7 @@ API changes
   remain untouched at their historical paths and are not auto-migrated because
   those paths do not encode the missing paradigm/suffix provenance; legacy
   artifacts therefore remain manually readable in place.
+- ``n_trials`` of :func:`moabb.analysis.plotting.dataset_bubble_plot` (and of the dataset dictionaries of :func:`moabb.datasets.utils.plot_datasets_grid` and :func:`moabb.datasets.utils.plot_datasets_cluster`) is now the number of trials of one subject over all its sessions, as in the summary tables; the bubble size no longer multiplies it by ``n_sessions``, which only sets the transparency (:gh:`1310` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 
 Requirements
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~
@@ -83,6 +84,7 @@ Requirements
 
 Bugs
 ~~~~
+- Fix the trial and session counts of the dataset summary tables and of :func:`moabb.analysis.plotting.dataset_bubble_plot`. ``#Trials / class`` counts every session and run of one subject, but the bubble size multiplied it again by ``#Sessions`` (BNCI2014_004 was drawn with 3,600 trials per subject instead of 720, EPFLP300 with 13,216 instead of 3,304), and ``scripts/generating_metainfo.py`` computed ``Total_trials`` as ``#Sessions`` x ``#Runs`` x the first subject's trials of all sessions x ``#Subj`` (62,208 instead of 5,184 for BNCI2014_001). The rows of BNCI2014_001, BNCI2014_002, BNCI2014_004, BNCI2015_001, Cho2017, Lee2019_MI, PhysionetMI, Schirrmeister2017, Shin2017A, Weibo2014, Zhou2016, MAMEM1, MAMEM2, MAMEM3, BI2013a, BI2014a, BI2015a, Cattan2019_VR, Huebner2017, Huebner2018 and Sosulski2019 now give the counts the loaders return, checked on every subject (Huebner2017 and Huebner2018 gave the trials of one run, 364 NT / 112 T, instead of 9,826 NT / 3,024 T and 10,920 NT / 3,360 T over three sessions). The rows of BCIComp2020UpperLimb, Brandl2020, Dreyer2023 (and A, B, C), Gao2026, GuttmannFlury2025_MI, GuttmannFlury2025_ME, GuttmannFlury2025_SSVEP, HefmiIch2025, Jeong2020, Ofner2017, Tavakolan2017, Wang2026Handwriting, Yang2025, Zhou2020 and Zuo2025 (a per-session or per-run ``#Trials / class``; Yang2025 and Wang2026Handwriting also list the 2 and 11 classes their loaders return by default) and of BNCI2015_004, Kaneshiro2015, Liu2025 and Shin2017B (a ``Total_trials`` multiplied by the sessions or runs, or missing the subjects) now follow the counts their documentation states. When subjects have different numbers of sessions, ``#Sessions`` now starts with that of a typical subject, the number the plots read: BI2013a ``1 (8 for subjects 1-7)`` instead of ``8 for subjects 1-7 else 1``, Sosulski2019 60 instead of 80, and BNCI2015_001, Gao2026, GuttmannFlury2025_*, Kaya2018, Liu2025, Ortiz2023, Peters2026, RomaniBF2025ERP and Thapa2025. The column definitions of :doc:`dataset_summary` state these conventions (:gh:`1310` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.Kodera2023` returning two sampling rates: the 14 subjects of the 2020-2021 recordings are at 500 Hz and the 15 of the 2021-2023 recordings at 1000 Hz (checked on every header of the archive), while ``METADATA`` said 500 Hz. Without a paradigm ``resample``, a call mixing both setups built epochs of 2001 and 4001 samples and stopped in ``np.concatenate``. By default all 29 subjects now return the nine shared channels at 500 Hz (the 1000 Hz recordings are resampled when loaded). The new ``cohort`` option returns one setup with its full montage: ``cohort="16ch"`` (code ``Kodera-16ch2023``) the 14 2020-2021 subjects with all 16 scalp channels at 500 Hz, ``cohort="9ch"`` (code ``Kodera-9ch2023``) the 15 2021-2023 subjects at the native 1000 Hz; a subject of the other setup raises a ``ValueError`` and downloads are shared. Cached ``Kodera2023`` epochs and results of subjects 3-10, 16, 17, 22, 23 and 27-29 computed at 1000 Hz must be deleted and recomputed (:gh:`1276` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.PerezBlanco2026` returning one run at another sampling rate: ``sub-09`` ``run-01`` is stored at about 1200 Hz (EDF header 1199.4 Hz) while the other 447 runs of the 45 subjects are at 512 Hz, so any paradigm call including subject 9 stopped in ``np.concatenate`` ("the array at index 0 has size 1281 and the array at index 2 has size 3000"). The loader now resamples any run that is not at 512 Hz to 512 Hz after locating its events. Cached ``PerezBlanco2026`` epochs and results of subject 9 must be deleted and recomputed (:gh:`XXXX` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix :class:`moabb.datasets.PerezBlanco2026` returning one run at another sampling rate: ``sub-09`` ``run-01`` is stored at about 1200 Hz (EDF header 1199.4 Hz) while the other 447 runs of the 45 subjects are at 512 Hz, so any paradigm call including subject 9 stopped in ``np.concatenate`` ("the array at index 0 has size 1281 and the array at index 2 has size 3000"). The loader now resamples any run that is not at 512 Hz to 512 Hz after locating its events. Cached ``PerezBlanco2026`` epochs and results of subject 9 must be deleted and recomputed (:gh:`1277` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
